[{"source":"codebase","severity":"note","category":"coverage-gap","title":"campus-half landing floor hardcodes literal 10 while the total EXPECTED was just made catalog-derived","location":"core/demand_test.odin:754","evidence":"EXPECTED := i64(stream_entries) * i64(surge.multiplier) * i64(WINDOW) // 2×1×10×WINDOW = 20×WINDOW\ntesting.expectf(t, campus_window_spawns >= 10*WINDOW*95/100,\n\t\t\"the campus half must land: in-window campus spawns %d < %d (10/tick × WINDOW × 0.95)\", campus_window_spawns, 10*WINDOW*95/100)","detail":"N5 made EXPECTED derive from the catalog (Σ streaming volumes × multiplier × WINDOW), but the campus half floor still hardcodes 10 (campus vol 1 × multiplier 10). A future campus-volume or multiplier re-tune silently mis-windows the campus floor — the exact drift N4/N5 prevent.","recommended_fix":"Derive the campus ask like EXPECTED: sum volumes of streaming entries whose source_role == .Campus, multiply by surge.multiplier × WINDOW × 95/100."},{"source":"codebase","severity":"note","category":"documentation","title":"usage() help text omits the new fold-check verb","location":"harness/main.odin:275","evidence":"//   odin run harness -- fold-check <prev-hash> <prev-tick1>\nfmt.eprintln(\"usage: harness run|save [demo...] [--stats-out <path>] | replay <demo> <log.bin> | drift-check | preview-check | stats-check <demo> | input-parity [save] | palcheck | map-preview <seed> [out.png]\")","detail":"The fold-check verb is dispatched (main.odin:142) and documented in the file header (line 22), but the runtime usage() string omits it, so `harness fold-check` with bad args prints help that does not mention the verb the user invoked.","recommended_fix":"Append `| fold-check <prev-hash> <prev-tick1>` to the usage() eprintln string."}]
